    "title": "RaunakGengiti2725/NUDT5-Inhibitor-Breast-Cancer-Discovery: Structure-Based and Machine Learning Discovery of NUDT5 Inhibitors for Breast Cancer",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19374517",
    "publication_date": "2026-04-01",
    "description": "<h2>Description</h2>\n<p>This release contains the complete computational pipeline for the discovery of novel NUDT5 inhibitors targeting estrogen receptor\u2013positive (ER+) breast cancer. The project integrates structure-based drug design, cheminformatics, and machine learning approaches to identify and prioritize potential therapeutic candidates.</p>\n<p>The workflow combines molecular fingerprinting (ECFP4), Tanimoto similarity screening, Glide SP/XP docking, MM-GBSA rescoring, and supervised learning using a random forest classifier. The pipeline is designed to operate effectively under low-data conditions, making it suitable for early-stage drug discovery.</p>\n<p>The dataset includes an initial compound library of approximately 18,400 molecules, which was filtered through the pipeline to yield 10 structurally diverse candidate inhibitors. These candidates exhibit favorable drug-like properties, including appropriate molecular weight, lipophilicity, and polar surface area.</p>\n<p>This repository provides all scripts, datasets, and results necessary to reproduce the analysis. It is intended to support transparency, reproducibility, and reuse in computational drug discovery research.</p>\n<h2>Contents</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>scripts/</code> \u2013 Pipeline implementation and analysis code</li>\n<li><code>data/</code> \u2013 Input compound libraries</li>\n<li><code>results/</code> \u2013 Final screened hits and outputs</li>\n<li><code>requirements.txt</code> \u2013 Python dependencies</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Keywords</h2>\n<p>NUDT5, breast cancer, drug discovery, molecular docking, machine learning, cheminformatics, in silico screening</p>\n<h2>License</h2>\n<p>Please refer to the repository for licensing details.</p>",
